  "reasoning": "The claim is accurate. In early 2023, researchers evaluated OpenAI's GPT-4 on the Uniform Bar Examination (UBE), demonstrating that the model comfortably passed the exam with scores exceeding the average human test-taker. While OpenAI originally reported a 90th percentile score, follow-up independent analyses (such as by legal researcher Eric Martinez) noted that when comparing against the full pool of test-takers rather than retakers, the score was approximately at the 68th percentile—which remains well above average. Subsequent advanced foundation models (such as GPT-4o and Claude 3.5 Sonnet) have consistently replicated and exceeded these benchmark passing performances.",
